# Git attribute patterns are case-sensitive, so the lowercase globs above do not
# match uppercase extensions. A file that slipped through got no LFS filter at
# all and checked out as the literal 132-byte pointer text instead of a model,
# which broke conway's rc regression gate deterministically (issue #52). These
# mirror every extension above -- not just the model formats -- so the next
# uppercase file added does not silently reintroduce it. Keep the two lists in
# sync when adding a format; they should always be the same length.
*.IFC filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text
*.STL filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text
*.OBJ filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text
*.STEP filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text
